  "id": "thepapertomb",
  "note": "THE PAPER TOMB: the Hall of Records, on Kessler Street one door north of Precinct 9.\n\nThe tile's prose: a squat civic building of poured concrete and tall dark windows. Chiselled above\nthe lintel, half-legible under decades of grime: HALL OF RECORDS · COLDWATER MUNICIPAL. A brass slot\nbeside the door reads DEPOSIT DEEDS HERE. The door stands open, as it usually does.\n\nSo it is a concrete block on a deep plinth under a heavy cornice. The front has a portico of two\nsquare piers carrying a lintel with HALL OF RECORDS cut into it in dark letters, the door open under\nit with a little light from inside, and the brass slot on the pier. Four tall narrow windows flank\nthe portico, dark, because nobody works late in a records hall. The flanks carry the same windows.\nGrime runs down from the cornice.\n\nPrecinct 9 is its opposite: lit, flagged and busy. Nothing on this building is on but the door.\n\nIt stands in for the `thepapertomb` arm (`replaces`), which stays in LEGACY_MODELS.",
  "pal": "ty_dam",
